From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:32:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(goldens): pin the opencode database read and codex's
 absolute rollout_path; declare the rest

Three grey edges on the transformation graph, pinned hermetically:
- tests/opencode_db.rs stores the opencode fixture as opencode 1.18.18
  stores a session (schema-1.18.18.sql, from a real opencode-stable.db),
  resolves the channel-named file, reads it with ConvoIO and compares the IR
  to the export read: no difference (12 messages, 45 parts).
- tests/codex_home_copy.rs resumes the codex golden into a temp home with
  codex-cli 0.162.1's threads table, copies CODEX_HOME, and pins that the
  copy's threads.rollout_path still names the original rollout (known
  defect; qualifier concern on register_codex_thread).
- upload for gemini/opencode/cursor is pinned in pathbase (pr/09) as the
  uploaded documents.
Declared unpinned with qualifier concerns: resume into gemini-cli (no
answered model turn), resume into Cursor.app (body never shown), the live
pathbase stored row. pr/18 records the piece.
